    "text": "<p><code>String</code>s, like <code>int</code>s, support a number of operations. A simple one is <code>+</code>, which appends, or <em>concatenates</em>, strings together. For example:</p>\n\n<p><iframe height=\"450px\" scrolling=\"no\" src=\"https://tech.io/playground-widget/b6bf759a164313c4cab47a2fff43aad549685/welcome/1084066/Conctenating%20Strings\" width=\"100%\"></iframe></p>\n\n<h3><span style=\"color: #cc0000;\">Do Now! </span>Which of the following options contain text that is part of the output? </h3>\n\n<p>(Hint: Consider <em>all</em> parts of the output, not just the values in the fields. Interpret each option <em>exactly</em> as it appears below, e.g. if you do not see that exact sequence of characters together, then it is not a part of the output.)</p>",
